.TH MUCOR 1 "October 2026" "mucor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mucor \- a minimal Debian package template
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mucor
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mucor
is a minimal Debian package template.

.PP
When invoked without arguments,
.B mucor
displays its usage information.
Exactly one option may be provided per invocation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the usage message, available options, and bug-reporting URL.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display the program name and version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B mucor
Display the usage information.
.TP
.B mucor \-\-help
Display the help message.
.TP
.B mucor \-h
Display the help message using the short option.
.TP
.B mucor \-\-version
Display the version information.
.TP
.B mucor \-v
Display the version using the short option.
.SH ERRORS
.B mucor
reports an error when more than one argument is provided
or when an unrecognized option is supplied.
.PP
When an error occurs, consult the help message for the
supported options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command returns successfully when the help or version
option is handled successfully.
.PP
The exit status for invalid arguments depends on the
error-handling implementation in the installed script.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
No environment variables are required by the documented
command-line interface.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs, request features, or submit issue reports at:
.PP
